---
import { ComicStrip } from "@toonstrip/astro";
import doc from "../../content/tldr-strip.json";
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<title>Comic strips in Astro — toonstrip example</title>
	</head>
	<body>
		<article>
			<h1>Embedding a live comic strip in an Astro post</h1>
			<p>
				This post is the integration test for <code>@toonstrip/astro</code> (M4 of the
				toonstrip dev plan). Below is a hand-written 3-panel strip — no AI involved in
				generating it, per the project's own non-goals.
			</p>
			<p>
				Everything below this paragraph is filler height, so the strip starts well below
				the fold. Scroll down to see it load: open devtools' Network tab first, and you
				should see no request for <code>@toonstrip/element</code> until the strip
				scrolls into view — that's <code>client:visible</code> at work.
			</p>
			<div style="height: 1400px;" aria-hidden="true"></div>
			<h2>The TL;DR</h2>
			<ComicStrip document={doc} packs={["comic-chat"]} client:visible />
			<p>That's the whole embed: a document, a pack name, and a client directive.</p>
		</article>
	</body>
</html>
